waves/RW-22/review-A.txt:3:- [discord-i18n/src/lib.rs](/home/user/orca/project/rust/crates/discord-i18n/src/lib.rs:646): `parse_fence` can panic on the valid UTF-8 input `"```\n"`. With no closing fence, `open_end` is `3`, then `rest[open_end + 1..]` slices at byte 4 of a 4-byte string. The markdown truncation test does not cover this exact input and does not catch unwinds. This violates the no-panic requirement for untrusted markdown.
waves/RW-22/review-A.txt:9:- [discord-i18n/src/lib.rs](/home/user/orca/project/rust/crates/discord-i18n/src/lib.rs:510): Russian cardinal selection uses `abs() as i64` and never returns `other` for fractions. For example, `1.5` is classified as `one` instead of CLDR `other`; negative values also lose their sign. The Russian plural tests cover only positive integers.
waves/RW-22/review-A.txt:15:The six message-key vectors and empty-input xxHash known answer are independent expected values. Real catalog counts and the `hPBScv` text are external checks when the local artifacts exist; the i18n catalog test skips unavailable files. Other checks are weaker: the Russian demo test verifies a constant against a formula beside that constant, and the markdown tests mostly assert normalized output from the same parser/renderer pair. They do not exercise the fence panic or adversarial link delimiters.
